#Common
app.name=Create an agent services account
app.name-alreadySubscribed=Agent services account
servicename.titleSuffix=- GOV.UK
#Connect agent services
start.not-signed-in.title=Copy across your existing Self Assessment clients to your agent services account
start.not-signed-in.p1=You need to sign in to your agent services account to use this service.

start.title=Add authorisations from Self Assessment clients
start.p1=We need to know all the agent codes you use to manage Self Assessment clients.
start.inset=Adding client authorisations to your agent services account does not change any of your existing permissions – it just means your clients do not have to authorise you again.
start.copied=You’ve already told us about these Government Gateway accounts:
start.table.caption=Codes already added to your agent services account
start.li.header=Telling HMRC your agent codes means:
start.li1=we can collect the client authorisations from your Self Assessment account and bring them into your agent services account
start.li2=your clients will not have to authorise you again for Making tax Digital for Income Tax
start.details.link=More information about Self Assessment agent codes
start.details1=These codes are given to you by HMRC so you can manage Self Assessment for your clients.
start.details2=You might only have one Self Assessment agent code – this happens if you manage all your Self Assessment clients under the same Government Gateway user ID.
start.details3=But there’s no limit to how many agent codes you can have.
start.details4=There’s no limit to how many agent codes you can have.
start.button.agent.code=Add an agent code
start.yes=Yes - I’ll sign in now
start.hint=You need to sign in with the relevant Government Gateway user ID to prove you have access to the account.
start.error.required=Select yes if you want to add your client authorisations

start.task-list.heading=Add Self Assessment authorisations
start.task-list.p1=This means:
start.task-list.li1=you’ll tell us which Government Gateway accounts you use to manage Self Assessment clients in your HMRC online services account
start.task-list.li2=we’ll add the Self Assessment authorisations to your agent services account
start.task-list.li3=clients who already authorise you for Self Assessment will not have to authorise you again for Making Tax Digital for Income Tax – this includes any new clients you take on under the same Government Gateway IDs
start.task-list.p2=Adding authorisations does not mean:
start.task-list.li4=you have to sign up your clients to Making Tax Digital for Income Tax yet
start.task-list.li5=you’ll lose any of your current access or permissions to manage Self Assessment for your clients in your HMRC online services account

